{
  "program": "CBACT01C",
  "caseId": "case08",
  "description": "The ten-record slice: the first ten records of the shipped fixture, which makes its line count the sharpest single check on the per-record block size. app/cbl/CBACT01C.cbl:L70-L87 displays every record TWICE - 1100-DISPLAY-ACCT-RECORD is performed from inside the '00' arm of the read paragraph at L96, so its eleven labelled field lines (L119-L129) and 49-hyphen separator (L130) precede the mainline's raw DISPLAY ACCOUNT-RECORD at L78 - giving 13 lines per record and 1 + (10 x 13) + 1 = 132 lines in all. That count alone falsifies the two off-by-one translations that matter here: a block emitted as twelve lines lands on 122 and one emitted as fourteen lands on 142, so either is reported before a single byte is compared. Sitting between case02, whose single record isolates one block, and case01, whose fifty pin the whole file, this case is exactly case01 truncated to its first ten records - expectedMessages 1 through 130 are byte-identical to case01's by construction, and the first 13 and the first 26 are byte-identical to case02's and case04's - so a difference reported here that case01 does not also report can only lie in how the input was narrowed, never in how a line was derived. The widths within a block are fixed by the labels: 25 characters of label including the terminating colon (L119-L129) followed immediately by the field's display form, giving 36, 26, 37, 37, 37, 35, 35, 35, 37, 37 and 35, then the 49-hyphen separator, then the raw 300-byte image. Two legacy oddities are preserved rather than tidied: ACCT-ADDR-ZIP is in the record and holds 'A000000000' in all ten rows, yet the paragraph never labels it, and ACCT-GROUP-ID is blank in all ten rows so its line ends in ten spaces. R1 caveat: the mandated name AccountBalanceJob performs no balance work whatsoever - the source Function header reads 'Read and print account data file' - and this case pins that by asserting all ten rows unchanged on the final-state channel while expectedWrites is empty, with expectedDatasets stating the row count and the width so an eleventh row could not appear unaccounted for. Record layout, taken mechanically from app/cpy/CVACT01Y.cpy as thirteen absolute zero-based spans over 300 bytes (practice B11): ACCT-ID 0/11, ACCT-ACTIVE-STATUS 11/1, ACCT-CURR-BAL 12/12, ACCT-CREDIT-LIMIT 24/12, ACCT-CASH-CREDIT-LIMIT 36/12, ACCT-OPEN-DATE 48/10, ACCT-EXPIRAION-DATE 58/10 (the copybook's own misspelling, preserved per I1), ACCT-REISSUE-DATE 68/10, ACCT-CURR-CYC-CREDIT 78/12, ACCT-CURR-CYC-DEBIT 90/12, ACCT-ADDR-ZIP 102/10, ACCT-GROUP-ID 112/10, FILLER 122/178 - summing to exactly 300. A PIC S9(10)V99 field occupies 12 bytes and not 13: it is zoned DISPLAY with the sign overpunched into the trailing byte, which is why every monetary value in these ten rows ends in '{' - the positive-zero overpunch, a correct byte rather than corrupt data, and never to be normalised to '0'. The fixture bytes are US-ASCII (practice B8) and the dataset is addressed by its ACCTFILE binding key rather than by any dataset name (G46); acctdata.txt matches its copybook width exactly, so this case declares no normalisation. Baseline provenance (practice B12): these expected values are STATICALLY DERIVED from the COBOL source read paragraph by paragraph, the copybook byte layout, the READACCT.jcl STEP05 DD contract - a bare EXEC PGM with no PARM, hence no job parameter - and rows 0 through 9 of the real ASCII fixture. Not one of them was captured from a live COBOL execution, and none was captured from a run of this Java translation either: running the legacy programs is empirically impossible in this environment, as AAP section 0.7.6 establishes with eight independently verified blockers, and the substitution of provenance is escalated as risk R-A rather than absorbed silently. Gates discharged: G15 (one of the twenty cases this program owns), G16 (seeded from the real app/data/ASCII fixture), G18 (the diff count must be zero), G19 (the 300-byte account record width), G21 (FILLER present and space-filled - every raw line is 300 bytes with 122-299 all spaces), G47 (the '00' open, the ten '00' reads and the '10' end-of-file on the eleventh, which is a normal boundary and not an error) and G51 (the job is driven at tasklet level with no JobLauncher and no HTTP layer in the path).",
